   "html_text": "Chaos is typically understood as a property of a dynamical system. A dynamical system is a deterministic mathematical model for how observable properties of a system evolve with time. Time can be either discrete or continuous. A one-dimensional dynamical system is called a map (though the literature sometimes deviates from this usage). As an example of a discrete map, imagine a rule where you place one penny on the first square of a checkerboard, two on the second square, three on the third squa",
